INSERT INTO feature VALUES('incremental-checking','incremental','Incremental checking',NULL,'implemented','notable',NULL,'An edit rejudges only the items whose consulted answers changed, matching a batch check; the language server''s recheck resumes the import closure instead of readmitting it, and lowers the document''s own source alone over the closure''s lowering, held once per process, sharing the closure''s plans rather than copying them; the closure''s origins are carried once per judgement, and each source''s node tables are forgotten once it is lowered, so the suspended lowering holds none of the closure''s; the closure''s scope tables are finished once when it is suspended, and the document''s finish extends them with its own. The closure is judged once and the document on a copy of its context, the program, settle report and spellings joined at the boundary. The incremental pass''s state after the closure''s items is led once per closure and root, and each revision is submitted after it, encoding and judging only its own items; the hover table types the document on the closure''s context. Each pass opens its context through the judgement''s own constructor, so it decides an item under the module''s pattern holes, reducts, forgetting maps and literal readers, as the judgement does. Each pass steps the module run''s own schedule of mutual blocks: it decides each member of a block in its block, adopts and takes no member alone, and refuses the block whole as the judgement does. An adopted item''s checked or synthesised type is seated as its judgement formed it, with no formation walk. An item the pass does not adopt takes the verdict and the support the revision''s own judgement gave it, and is seated as an adopted item is, so a revision decides each changed item once. The enforcing build checks that the pass holds each answer the judgement read of an item before it takes the item. A refused item''s checkpoint keeps the failure the judgement read as content, each node outside the item at its place under a root of the item or of an item it consulted and with the path to each node of the item it holds, so a seat builds the refusal and its failure again in another arena over the item''s own nodes; an opaque item keeps none. An item its judgement entered elaborated keeps in its checkpoint each part the table holds in another form than the item writes it — the judged body, which is its definition, the declared type the table records, the stage signature and the following position — the body and the type as content that a seat mints again in another arena; an opaque item keeps none. An item whose judgement elaborated a nested computation of its body, or suspended its verdict, keeps that report in its checkpoint. Each node of the report stands at its place in the item''s walk, in the judged body''s table or in the report''s own table. A seat builds the elaboration and the suspension again in another arena from these places; an opaque item keeps none. A copy''s first judgement resumes from what an earlier copy of its document recorded — another connection''s copy, else the last one let go — whatever its text. The kernel readmission resumes the leading declarations a revision shares with the one admitted before it, a session holding its own runs past the closure, so a revision that changes no declaration offers the kernel none; the record it resumes freezes the kernel environment it keeps, so each resume shares the record''s arena and copies only the nodes it mints. The program a judged closure''s documents continue is frozen once, so each revision copies only the IL rows it focuses itself. A revision whose lowering moves no node of the one judged before it, as a comment''s does, takes that judgement''s verdicts rather than judging again, and settles and spells again at its own spans. A keystroke lays its document out over the path imports its last judgement''s parse read rather than parsing it again; a judgement whose parse reads others is laid out again, and stands when that lay-out closes it over the same closure, else is judged again.','core-incremental','crates/core-incremental/tests/incremental.rs crates/core-incremental/tests/recursive_data.rs crates/core-incremental/src/session/tests.rs crates/core-incremental/src/failure/tests.rs crates/surface-session/tests/session.rs crates/surface-session/tests/checkpoint.rs crates/surface-session/tests/incremental.rs crates/surface-session/tests/trace.rs crates/surface-dispatcher/tests/corpus.rs crates/surface-lsp/tests/session.rs crates/surface-lsp/src/server.rs crates/core-checker-bridge/src/bridge/tests.rs crates/surface-lowering/tests/namespace.rs crates/surface-lowering-base/src/table.rs crates/surface-dispatcher/src/compose.rs crates/core-checker-base/tests/recursive_data.rs crates/surface-dispatcher/src/component.rs crates/kernel-term/src/arena.rs crates/kernel-core/src/environment.rs crates/core-sequent/src/il/tests.rs',NULL,NULL);
